## The magistrates
Matters you cannot settle yourself — a theft, a debt in dispute, a wrong one villager lays at another's door — go before the magistrates in Salem Town. They sit each day at noon, read what passed in the village, and send word of their ruling to everyone the matter concerns; their ruling ends it. You may bring up to 2 new matters a day with bring_before_magistrates, naming the villagers concerned and saying what the matter is.
## The town's works
The windlass at the Well by the Mill is down — nobody can drink or draw water there until it is mended. The town has posted 12 coins for the mending; any hand seeking work may take it on.
The storm has torn at the General Store — it can take in no new stock, and its work goes slowly, until it is mended. The town chest cannot pay for the mending just now.
No one hires for the town's works or shares out the pay — the town pays each posted sum to the one hand who does that work.

Weigh what's in front of you — obligations and pressing needs come before idle matters. Choose one action, then call done() when nothing pressing remains.
